sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as Passenger
  participant A as API
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  participant P as Payment provider
  U->>A: POST booking + Idempotency-Key
  A->>D: Begin; lock idempotency/quota; select seats
  D->>D: Constraint-protected holds + reservation + payment intent + outbox
  D-->>A: Commit hold
  A->>P: Create payment session (after commit)
  P-->>A: Session reference
  A-->>U: PAYMENT_PENDING + expiry
  U->>P: Complete provider checkout
  P->>A: Signed success callback
  A->>D: Verify, dedupe, lock and confirm reservation/allocation
  D-->>A: Commit ledger, ticket/PNR and outbox
  A-->>P: Acknowledge durable event

sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as Passenger
  participant A as API
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  participant P as Provider
  U->>A: Create booking
  A->>D: Commit hold and pending payment intent
  A->>P: Create payment session
  P-->>U: Payment declined
  P->>A: Signed failure callback (may be delayed)
  A->>D: Dedupe event; mark payment failed; release hold
  D-->>A: Commit
  A-->>U: Failed / released; retry requires new booking

sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as Passenger
  participant A as API
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  U->>A: POST booking key K, payload H
  A->>D: Insert unique principal+K; create booking
  D-->>A: Commit result R
  A-->>U: Return R
  U->>A: Retry key K, payload H after timeout
  A->>D: Read idempotency record
  D-->>A: Same hash, stored result R
  A-->>U: Return same R; no duplicate allocation

sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant P as Provider
  participant A as Webhook API
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  participant W as Reconciler
  P--xA: Success callback delayed / delivery unavailable
  Note over D: Reservation remains PAYMENT_PENDING; no false confirmation
  W->>D: Find aged UNKNOWN/PENDING payment
  W->>P: Query provider status
  P-->>W: Verified succeeded status
  W->>D: Lock payment/hold; validate amount and hold/inventory
  alt Inventory still safely held
    D->>D: Commit SUCCEEDED + CONFIRMED + ticket/outbox
  else Hold expired or berth reallocated
    D->>D: Record paid exception and refund/recovery obligation
  end

sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as Passenger
  participant A as API
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  participant P as Provider
  U->>A: Cancel reservation (idempotency key)
  A->>D: Lock reservation; evaluate versioned rule
  D->>D: Commit CANCELLED + release inventory + refund obligation + outbox
  A->>P: Request refund after commit
  P-->>A: Refund reference / pending
  A->>D: Persist refund result idempotently
  A-->>U: Cancellation committed; refund status pending/known

sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant W as Waitlist worker
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  participant U as Passenger
  W->>D: Lock next eligible queue entry (SKIP LOCKED)
  W->>D: Recheck policy, passenger eligibility and available inventory
  alt Eligible and inventory available
    W->>D: Create bounded offer/hold and outbox event
    D-->>W: Commit
    W-->>U: Notify promotion offer / next action
  else Not eligible or no inventory
    W->>D: Record policy outcome and continue/stop per rule version
  end
